&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively contribute to the development and growth of the Procurement department by bringing fresh perspectives and procurement expertise to internal stakeholders (spend cube analysis, KPI definition, business cases, TCO analysis, category approach, action plans/roadmaps)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage end-to-end procurement projects autonomously including RFI, RFP, and direct negotiations across all spend categories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate all internal and external stakeholders involved in the purchasing process to ensure compliance with internal and external policies and regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal stakeholders in implementing and maintaining a Supplier Relationship Management (SRM) approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to daily Procurement operations including contract management tool updates, savings reporting, and corporate card management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with the G&amp;amp;A department (Finance &amp;amp; Accounting, Legal, Compliance, Security)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in integrating artificial intelligence into daily processes, including creating AI agents to automate recurring tasks and optimize team productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
